Design pattern used: OBSERVER and COMPOSITE.

Observer: T used the observer to subscribe customers to black friday deals. 
this is useful because it effectively notify those who are subscribed and those who were not.

Composite: this pattern was used because i needed the category to be able to contain other subcategories
and products (the leaf).
this pattern help my code to be efficient in many ways
the first step, the hierarchy of the composite design is the blackfriday deal being able to contain
other subcategories like clothing and electronics. 
the second step is each of those categories contain their own products such as headphones or jackets.

how my code works:
I have an abstract class for the product to structure what my product should have. (a name, a price, 
to display.) Then in my product class I implemented concrete functions. Which get overrided through
concrete products made in main. 

The customer class defines a customer. each customer has a name and a function to recieve notifications.
The notification is notified when a subscriber is subscribe to the blackfriday deal. 

Blackfridaydeal allows flexibility with adding removing subscribers on top of notifying subscribers.
additionally, it make sure only every individual customer can subscribe once. 
the Blackfridaydeal class also logs rather a customer is currently subscribed or not.
